            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "For this bit `__ANDROID_API__` and `__ANDROID_MIN_SDK_VERSION__` are reportedly the same thing, except `__ANDROID_API__` is the older deprecated version. Presumably there's some old systems which only have `__ANDROID_API__` but I don't immediately know how old.\n\nIt seems safest to check them both but they should be the same.",
            "commit_id": "3b3f41ec3d0aff46208646d75021b46aabe2e68b",
            "created_at": "2026-10-03T23:08:09Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -4,9 +4,18 @@\n #if !defined(CYTHON_CCOMPLEX)\n   #if defined(__cplusplus)\n     #define CYTHON_CCOMPLEX 1\n-  #elif (defined(_Complex_I) && !defined(_MSC_VER)) || ((defined (__STDC_VERSION__) && __STDC_VERSION__ >= 201112L) && !defined(__STDC_NO_COMPLEX__) && !defined(_MSC_VER))\n-    // <complex.h> should exist since C99, but only C11 defines a test to detect it.\n-    // MSVC defines \"_Complex_I\" but not \"_Complex\". See https://github.com/cython/cython/issues/5512\n+  #elif defined(_MSC_VER)\n+    // MSVC never implements the C standard complex numbers. See https://github.com/cython/cython/issues/5512\n+    #define CYTHON_CCOMPLEX 0\n+  #elif (defined(__ANDROID_MIN_SDK_VERSION__) && __ANDROID_MIN_SDK_VERSION__ < 26) || (defined(__ANDROID_API__) && __ANDROID_API__ < 26)",
